rsz: collect startpoint metrics for a progress row only when the phase steers by them

Candidate fix from the repair_timing runtime study; not upstreamed.
Retires at the bump onto an OpenROAD that carries it or a better
version of it.

With -verbose, repair_timing prints a progress row every ten passes and
once per endpoint. Each row calls collectViolatingStartpoints(), which
walks every vertex in the timing graph and reads a slack per startpoint,
to fill the StTNS column. On the asap7 designs where repair grinds, the
rows are 28-29% of the whole repair_timing wall (riscv32i floorplan
9.5 of 33 s, cts 10.7 of 38 s), measured with patches/0066.

Chesterton's Fence: StTNS arrived with the startpoint-driven phases
(STARTPOINT_FANOUT), whose objective it is, and printing it on every row
lets the two objectives be compared as a run proceeds. For the default
pipeline (LEGACY then LAST_GASP) it is a spectator column. This keeps the
column, fills it only when the phase steers by startpoints, prints "-"
otherwise, and leaves the final row -- printed once -- carrying it for
every phase. No move decision reads it; the result is unchanged.

diff --git a/src/rsz/src/policy/SetupLegacyBase.cc b/src/rsz/src/policy/SetupLegacyBase.cc
index de530b3b6c..9a2a5f060b 100644
--- a/src/rsz/src/policy/SetupLegacyBase.cc
+++ b/src/rsz/src/policy/SetupLegacyBase.cc
@@ -884,14 +884,22 @@ void SetupLegacyBase::printProgress(const int iteration,
     return;
   }
 
-  // StTNS is printed in every progress row, so collect startpoints only when a
-  // row is actually emitted.
-  target_collector_->collectViolatingStartpoints();
+  // The startpoint column is the objective of the startpoint-driven
+  // phases (STARTPOINT_FANOUT) and a spectator everywhere else. Collecting
+  // it walks every vertex in the graph and reads a slack per startpoint,
+  // on every row, and the endpoint-driven phases print a row per
+  // endpoint. So it is collected only when the phase steers by it; the
+  // other phases print the column blank and the final row, printed once,
+  // still carries it.
+  const bool show_startpoint_metrics = use_startpoint_metrics;
+  std::string st_tns_field = "-";
+  if (show_startpoint_metrics) {
+    target_collector_->collectViolatingStartpoints();
+    st_tns_field = delayAsString(target_collector_->getTns(true), 1, sta_);
+  }
 
   const sta::Slack wns = target_collector_->getWns();
-  const sta::Slack st_tns = target_collector_->getTns(true);
   const sta::Slack en_tns = target_collector_->getTns(false);
-  const bool show_startpoint_metrics = use_startpoint_metrics;
   const sta::Pin* worst_pin
       = target_collector_->getWorstPin(show_startpoint_metrics);
 
@@ -917,7 +925,7 @@ void SetupLegacyBase::printProgress(const int iteration,
       totalMoves(MoveType::kSwapPins),
       area_growth_percent,
       delayAsString(wns, 3, sta_),
-      delayAsString(st_tns, 1, sta_),
+      st_tns_field,
       delayAsString(en_tns, 1, sta_),
       std::max(0, target_collector_->getNumViolatingEndpoints()),
       worst_pin != nullptr ? network_->pathName(worst_pin) : "");
